From: WorkBuddy <wb@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:25:00 +0800
Subject: [OHOS] paint-holding: transparent fallback ONLY at view creation (rev2)

rev1 of this patch also set the fallback surface background to transparent
inside DidNavigate(). That was a regression: during navigation the aura
surface gap then reveals the shell theme color, which flashes BLACK against
light web pages in dark mode. Measured on device (address-bar search ->
load, three navigations): full-screen mean brightness dropped 0.68 -> 0.08
(~200 ms) each time in dark theme, i.e. a visible black flash.

The per-page fallback background must keep tracking the OUTGOING page's
root_background_color (UpdateBackgroundColor), so the navigation gap matches
the previous page instead of the shell theme. Forcing it transparent during
navigation breaks that and introduces the black flash.

rev2 therefore keeps ONLY the Init default change (SK_ColorWHITE ->
SK_ColorTRANSPARENT), which fixes the cold-start / new-tab white flash
(GetBackgroundColor() is empty at view creation) and does not touch same-view
web->web navigation, where the gap should stay the previous page's color.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_aura.cc
@@ -3082,11 +3082,15 @@ void RenderWidgetHostViewAura::CreateAuraWindow(aura::client::WindowType type) {
   aura::client::SetFocusChangeObserver(window_, this);
   display_observer_.emplace(this);

   window_->SetType(type);
   window_->Init(ui::LAYER_SURFACE);
-  SkColor4f background_color = SkColor4f::FromColor(
-      GetBackgroundColor() ? *GetBackgroundColor() : SK_ColorWHITE);
+  // Default to transparent so the cold-start / new-tab gap reveals the
+  // shell's themed background instead of flashing opaque white. The ArkUI
+  // XComponent hosting the web surface is already Color.Transparent, so the
+  // themed background shows through until the first frame paints.
+  SkColor4f background_color = SkColor4f::FromColor(
+      GetBackgroundColor() ? *GetBackgroundColor() : SK_ColorTRANSPARENT);
   window_->layer()->SetFillsBoundsOpaquely(background_color.isOpaque());
   window_->layer()->AsSurface()->SetFallbackBackgroundColor(background_color);
   UpdateFrameSinkIdRegistration();
 }
